    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 5,
        "sourceEnd": 201,
        "text": "Welcome back to Campus Voices. I'm Mia Chen, and today we're talking about how students check information online. With me is Daniel Wu, a second-year journalism student. Daniel, thanks for coming.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "72f36533e9db04da7fd7c6652a519e78147fca8e397a8d107eb0e32af7b4f92b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 210,
        "sourceEnd": 411,
        "text": "Thanks for having me, Mia. So, the other day I was reading a news story about a new study on coffee and sleep. The headline said 'Coffee causes insomnia in all students.' I thought that was too strong.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "35fcc8f3f701c15045c7ea99a100fba1950c27d489b983e4dc8080f3be8a4ebd",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 417,
        "sourceEnd": 440,
        "text": "Right. What did you do?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "43b80dc2dea3093e61207c8c374e805aa0402d249616ea388c44784dd9308b43",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 449,
        "sourceEnd": 726,
        "text": "Well, first I looked for the original study. The article said 'researchers claim' but didn't name the university. I found the study on a university website. It said 'some students who drank coffee after 6 p.m. had trouble sleeping.' Not all students. And it was only 50 people.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "7b2a4a730c2975bc5786c2744f5982233b8a12d35b2f6583c6a0f15bef2cbdfa",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 732,
        "sourceEnd": 773,
        "text": "So the headline exaggerated the findings.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "adf0c4b0b1ba4846d1d8b279b796b58cbe497be6b04dd140e9e29aa340b6bd10",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 782,
        "sourceEnd": 950,
        "text": "Exactly. The journalist used the verb 'claim' which suggests doubt, but then the headline said 'causes' which is very strong. Also, they didn't mention the sample size.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "216a0215b7b435adc7a8221999f4d1ef7c59c42cb62636100cd90834ee664da6",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 956,
        "sourceEnd": 1035,
        "text": "What about social media? Do you think most students check facts before sharing?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "e26d16586a34feda40442b98cc85211c120ccb2e0dfbca6c25b110245e42906a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1044,
        "sourceEnd": 1273,
        "text": "Honestly, I think most students don't check. I read a survey from our own university that said 70 percent of students share news without reading the full article. But that's just one survey. I wouldn't say 'all students' do that.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "b299b55c1e052e4cf1cd1d2477c892eb471a6c3600ebf9fa3b358eb34a951140",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1279,
        "sourceEnd": 1330,
        "text": "So you're careful with words like 'all' and 'most'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "1fe604433fb2aba8e5cf48201a7199c00f5afd90097c80594928a3d8cd6b30f7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1339,
        "sourceEnd": 1536,
        "text": "Yes. In journalism, we say 'some' means a few, 'most' means more than half but not all, and 'all' means every single one. If you use 'all' when you only have evidence for 'some', that's misleading.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "3f048c2fba999e12fc4626e40a035600e1903cf81e90b95470eaf361bb31d05b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1542,
        "sourceEnd": 1601,
        "text": "Can you give an example of how to report speech accurately?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "6db87a9b6d0ef4229bec3cb44ac88681fbabb3de1501fc9b48f7980a0faa28df",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1610,
        "sourceEnd": 1840,
        "text": "Sure. If a scientist says 'I think there might be a link,' you shouldn't write 'Scientist says there is a link.' You should write 'The scientist suggested there might be a link.' The verb 'suggest' is softer than 'say' or 'claim'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "7e8648a03010164cb11a56cdef52f75ece2e14eb5df3053d203d7293e5fc1a27",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 1846,
        "sourceEnd": 1886,
        "text": "So the choice of reporting verb matters.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "148b012bc5c5db7191a57756b7c2278d601b1d86b009b9cfb154cbfc3b57b020",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 1895,
        "sourceEnd": 2038,
        "text": "A lot. 'Claim' can suggest the person is not reliable. 'State' is neutral. 'Admit' suggests they did something wrong. So we need to be careful.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "b3cb8a98ec8e9bd49797bf2e5ffb30db1aa620977f1146ce0bf06445095fd375",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2044,
        "sourceEnd": 2086,
        "text": "What advice do you have for our listeners?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "110dabf9afa06fe718ab5b268e5fd23547e15ea4af2c5479dfcf8ffc3b9c5855",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2095,
        "sourceEnd": 2290,
        "text": "Check the original source. Look at the numbers. Ask: does the evidence support the words 'all' or 'most'? And when you share, use careful language. Say 'some studies suggest' not 'studies prove'.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "750f6a76c09845d88c1742831dbc9ffa08598d9a617210333413cd0cfb15ef6f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "mia",
        "speaker": "Mia",
        "sourceStart": 2296,
        "sourceEnd": 2325,
        "text": "Great advice. Thanks, Daniel.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-SoniaNeural",
        "textHash": "473394b89a610c3704878bb51a19f734992d541dff8c0aa6f25b5d5dff76880f",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      },
      {
        "role": "daniel",
        "speaker": "Daniel",
        "sourceStart": 2334,
        "sourceEnd": 2349,
        "text": "Thank you, Mia.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-GB-RyanNeural",
        "textHash": "f152acfa0e8aca6d641683b4b3693682434d8511eda44908bd68109e268e822d",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.65
      }
    ]
  },
